PURPOSE
Evaluate trajectories of a device moving in a flow field, including where it
starts, whether and when it reaches a destination, and the conditions or
consumption associated with the journey.

IDENTIFIER CONVENTION
Requirement identifiers use REQ-<SCOPE>-<TOPIC>. SCOPE is GEN for general
requirements, DRONE for the city-drone scenario, and PILL for the pill-in-pipe
scenario. TOPIC describes the requirement subject. Identifiers are independent
of requirement ordering and should remain unchanged when requirements are
inserted or reordered.

GENERAL REQUIREMENTS

REQ-GEN-FLOW
The program shall evaluate device trajectories in a supplied or calculated
flow field.

REQ-GEN-REGIONS
The program shall accept a start region and a destination region. Each region
may be specified as a domain or a patch.

REQ-GEN-START-LOCATIONS
The program shall evaluate trajectories from multiple candidate starting
locations within the specified start region and identify the starting
locations that meet the scenario's destination and performance criteria.

REQ-GEN-OUTCOMES
The program shall report trajectory outcomes, including destination
attainment and travel time, for the evaluated starting locations.

REQ-GEN-DEVICE-MODELS
The program shall support scenario-specific device models: a controlled
vehicle model for the drone scenario and a physical-motion model for the pill
scenario.

USER STORY 1: DRONE IN THE CITY

REQ-DRONE-OPENFOAM-FLOW
The program shall support a city flow field calculated using OpenFOAM.

REQ-DRONE-CITY-GEOMETRY
The program shall support city-building geometry harvested from open sources.

REQ-DRONE-CONTROL-MODEL
The program shall model the drone using a control model.

REQ-DRONE-FASTEST-ARRIVAL
Given a specified start patch and destination domain or patch, the program
shall evaluate drone trajectories from candidate locations on the start patch
and identify the location or locations with the fastest arrival at the
destination.

REQ-DRONE-BATTERY-CONSUMPTION
The program shall report battery consumption for each evaluated drone
trajectory and for the fastest-arrival result.

USER STORY 2: PILL IN THE CHAMBER

REQ-PILL-STL-GEOMETRY
The program shall accept geometry supplied as an STL file.

REQ-PILL-START-LOCATIONS
Given a specified start domain or patch and destination domain or patch, the
program shall evaluate pill trajectories from candidate starting locations.

REQ-PILL-PHYSICAL-MODEL
The program shall model pill motion according to the applicable physical
laws.

REQ-PILL-TIME-LIMIT
The program shall use 100 times the fluid residence time in the domain as the
maximum evaluation time for deciding whether the pill reaches its destination
in a reasonable time.

REQ-PILL-REACHABLE-START-LOCATIONS
The program shall identify starting locations from which the pill reaches
the destination within the maximum evaluation time.

REQ-PILL-STUCK-LOCATIONS
The program shall identify starting locations where the pill becomes stuck,
defined as its trajectory velocity falling below a specified low-velocity
criterion. The criterion shall be an input to the evaluation.

REQ-PILL-TRAJECTORY-OUTCOMES
The program shall report the travel time or stuck outcome for each evaluated
pill starting location.